The files under capture/ started from the SolarisEngine snapshot at upstream commit
78f23e7a5f120e28df4819b7cc8b91ea0806ca17 (2026-07-23, "pin webpack to 5.108.4 for prismarine-viewer-colalab install").
Every file under capture/ that differs from that commit, or is not in it, was modified or added for this repository;
capture/MODIFICATIONS.md lists them.
The modified upstream files are mainly in controller/, postprocess/, server/episode-manager-plugin/ and camera/, plus
generate_compose.py, run.sh, regenerate_skin_cache.py and README.md. What was changed and added:
- a Windows-native runtime and a headless Linux runtime;
- a camera capture mod that records the rendered camera pose and FOV of every frame, plus a pose link;
- world-state logging that replays exactly;
- per-frame player state;
- 45+ episode types;
- local skins;
- verification tools.

The Minecraft content visible in the gameplay images (docs/assets/ and capture/docs/source/_static/) is (c) Mojang /
Microsoft, shown under the Minecraft Usage Guidelines, and is not covered by the Apache License.

Not included in this repository. Each item is obtained by the user and is under its own terms:
- Minecraft, including the client and server jars, assets, block models and default skins. Mojang; Minecraft EULA. Read from the user's own installation.
- Paper. Downloaded by the capture setup.
- ProtocolLib, SkinsRestorer. Downloaded by scripts/setup_assets.py; see THIRD_PARTY.md.
- Fabric Loader. Fetched by the capture mod build and the client install.
- Mineflayer and other npm packages. See capture/package.json.
- nvdiffrast. Optional GPU rasteriser, installed separately.

THIRD_PARTY.md lists these and the few third-party files that are stored in this repository.
